course: dictionary
lesson: 13741
title: Interaction: things that act on each other
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interaction happens when two or more people or things act on each other, talk or work together. The word is a noun, so you can have an interaction, or many interactions. Look for clues in the sentence to find its meaning. «The bees had a busy interaction with the flowers.» The bees visit the flowers, so the two are acting on each other.
explain: Interaction is also used in science. «The fox and the rabbit are linked by their interaction in the food web.» Here the word shows how living things affect each other. Ask yourself: who is acting on whom? That question helps you unlock the meaning.
explain: «Our class had a friendly interaction with the visiting author.» The word shows that people talked and listened to each other. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Our class had a friendly talking and listening with the visiting author" makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: An interaction is when two or more people or things act on each other.
fact: «Interaction» is a noun: an interaction, interactions.
fact: In science, an interaction can be between chemicals in a reaction, or between living things in a food web.
fact: In medicine, a drug interaction is when two medicines affect each other in the body.
fact: In computing, an interaction is when a person acts on a screen or game and the screen or game responds.
exercise: «The bees and the flowers have an interaction: the bees carry pollen and the flowers feed them.» What is an interaction? | A kind of insect | * When two things act on each other | A type of flower
exercise: «Ella had a friendly interaction with the new girl at school.» What does interaction mean here? | * Talking and working together | Running away from someone | Drawing a picture alone | A type of school bag
exercise: Which of these is an example of a social interaction? | A tree that never moves | A rock sitting still on the hill | * Two friends chatting and sharing a game | A cloud floating alone in the sky
test: What is a drug interaction? | A tablet that tastes nice | * When two medicines affect each other in the body | A name for a doctor | A bad mood after lunch
test: In a food web, what does an interaction show? | A shopping list for the week | * How animals affect each other, like a fox eating a rabbit | A web spun only by spiders | Plants growing alone with no help
exam: In computing, what is an interaction with a game? | * When a player acts on the game and the game responds | A list of game rules | A game that is switched off | A type of computer mouse
